        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "854ae350-02b3-5971-8e18-b76a1d640021",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: English National Ballet\n- Places: London Coliseum, Royal Albert Hall, St. Martin's Lane, central London\n- People: Alina Cojocaru, Frank Matcham, Oswald Stoll\n- Roles: principal dancer, theatrical architect, impresario\n\nFacts:\n- The London Coliseum opened on 24 December 1904 as the London Coliseum Theatre of Varieties.\n- Frank Matcham designed the London Coliseum for the impresario Oswald Stoll.\n- The London Coliseum, also known as the Coliseum Theatre, is a theatre on St. Martin's Lane in central London.\n- The London Coliseum was built as one of London's largest and most luxurious family variety theatres.\n- As of November 2013, Alina Cojocaru was a principal dancer with the English National Ballet.\n- The English National Ballet regularly performs seasons at the London Coliseum.\n- The English National Ballet has been noted for specially staged performances at the Royal Albert Hall.",
